From b559b78b321f7aa3044b68fbc0894221e064115f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 12:51:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 249/249] patch 0249 -- gus-5 (#40): StopAllVoices across the
 .pat song boundary

MidiBackendGus::on_song_start() tears down the prior song's voices before
freeing/re-uploading the .pat region, but its per-voice loop only covers the
music voice pool (_num_voices). Looping Pixtone SFX voices (e.g. CRITTER_FLY)
are allocated from a separate GF1 voice range the music backend does not own,
so a looping SFX survives a song change and keeps driving the card while we
PIO-poke the new song's instruments -- the same contention window patch 0248
closes for note dispatch.

Call SDL_DOSGusStopAllVoices() (sdl-pg gus-5 export, SDL/0112) at the top of
on_song_start to quiesce every GF1 voice -- music + SFX -- before the upload.
SFX DRAM is preserved by the persist_mark, so silenced SFX replay after the
song change; only in-flight playback is cut, correct across a scene transition.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/sound/MidiBackendGus.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sound/MidiBackendGus.cpp b/src/sound/MidiBackendGus.cpp
index 7a233cd6..ab6c36cc 100644
--- a/src/sound/MidiBackendGus.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/MidiBackendGus.cpp
@@ -628,6 +628,15 @@ void MidiBackendGus::on_song_start()
   // song's voices, free its DRAM, then pre-upload exactly the instruments the
   // new song references so the IRQ note path only ever touches resident DRAM.
 
+  // patch 0249 (#40, gus-5): quiesce EVERY GF1 voice -- including looping SFX
+  // voices (e.g. CRITTER_FLY) allocated by the Pixtone path, which the music
+  // pool loop below does NOT own. A looping SFX surviving a song change would
+  // keep driving the card while we PIO-poke the new song's .pat instruments
+  // (the contention window). StopAllVoices is the only call that reaches the
+  // SFX voice range; the per-voice music loop below still clears engine-side
+  // _voices[].active bookkeeping (StopAllVoices is a hardware-only sweep).
+  SDL_DOSGusStopAllVoices();
+
   for (int v = 0; v < _num_voices; ++v)
   {
     SDL_DOSGusStopVoice(v);
